IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Kentucky Transitional Assistance Program (KTAP, Kentucky's TANF cash assistance): KRS 205.193, 205.200 and 205.210 with
-- the standards of need and amount in 921 KAR 2:016 -- the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Written in the texts' own actors and terms: the "applicant" and "recipient", the "needy child", the "benefit group",
-- the "cabinet" (for health and family services), the "payment maximum", "standard of need" and "gross income limit", the
-- "ratable reduction", the "work expense standard deduction".
--
-- Edition: Kentucky Revised Statutes (LRC; enactments through the 2026 Regular Session; database updated 10/19/2026),
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/krs-205-public-assistance-ktap-ssp.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19 UTC); and
-- 921 KAR 2:016 as current on the LRC register on 2026-10-19 (eff. 2-16-2023), deposited in the sibling subject
-- ../../../kentucky-administrative-regulations-921-kar-2-015-and-2-016-state-supplementation-and-ktap-standards/
-- registers/source-bundle/921-kar-2-016-ktap-standards-of-need-and-amount.txt.
--
-- The applicant's seat questions are in ky-ktap-seat.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `KTAP`

§§ `921 KAR 2:016 Section 9 -- the standards`

-- Section 9(2)(a): "Number of Eligible Persons | Payment Maximum | Standard of Need": 1 $372 $481; 2 $450 $552; 3 $524
-- $631; 4 $656 $710; 5 $766 $790; 6 $864 $869; 7 or more $964 $948. (2)(b) "Maximum Gross Income Limits": 1 $890;
-- 2 $1,021; 3 $1,169; 4 $1,315; 5 $1,462; 6 $1,608; 7 or more $1,754.
-- Section 9(6): "To the extent funds are available, the payment maximum, gross income limit, and standard of need shall
-- be the amount established in this section in addition to cost of living adjustments determined by the Social Security
-- Administration that have taken place beginning in 2023". The adjustments are not deposited; the cabinet's factor is an
-- input (1 for the printed figures).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      f1 IS A NUMBER, f2 IS A NUMBER, f3 IS A NUMBER, f4 IS A NUMBER, f5 IS A NUMBER, f6 IS A NUMBER, f7 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`by group size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF n AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        IF n EQUALS 1 THEN f1
        IF n EQUALS 2 THEN f2
        IF n EQUALS 3 THEN f3
        IF n EQUALS 4 THEN f4
        IF n EQUALS 5 THEN f5
        IF n EQUALS 6 THEN f6
        OTHERWISE f7

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `adjustment factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`payment maximum` n `adjustment factor` MEANS `adjustment factor` TIMES (`by group size` n 372 450 524 656 766 864 964)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `adjustment factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`standard of need` n `adjustment factor` MEANS `adjustment factor` TIMES (`by group size` n 481 552 631 710 790 869 948)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `adjustment factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`gross income limit` n `adjustment factor` MEANS `adjustment factor` TIMES (`by group size` n 890 1021 1169 1315 1462 1608 1754)

§§ `921 KAR 2:016 Section 3 -- resources`

-- Section 3(2): "The total amount of resources reserved by a benefit group shall not be in excess of $10,000 in liquid
-- assets", excluding the resources listed in (3).
GIVEN `countable liquid assets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the resource limitation` IF `countable liquid assets` AT MOST 10000

§§ `921 KAR 2:016 Sections 4 and 5 -- income`

-- Section 5(3): "(a) Work expense standard deduction of 175 dollars for full-time and part-time employment; (b) [a
-- dependent care disregard of not more than $175 a month per individual for full-time employment, $150 for part-time,
-- $200 for a child under two, where the caregiver is not the parent, guardian or in the benefit group]; (c), (d) [child
-- support received and retained before notice of eligibility, or assigned and forwarded to the cabinet]; (e) For six (6)
-- months, the first fifty (50) percent of earned income not already deducted for each member of the benefit group". (4):
-- the (a), (b) and (e) deductions do not apply for a month the individual reduced, ended or refused employment in the
-- prior 30 days without good cause, or failed to report an increase in earnings within ten days without good cause.
DECLARE `Monthly income` HAS
    `gross earned income`                           IS A NUMBER
    `employed members of the benefit group`         IS A NUMBER
    `dependent care disregard`                      IS A NUMBER  -- (3)(b), within its caps
    `in the six months of the fifty percent disregard` IS A BOOLEAN -- (3)(e)
    `earnings deductions lost under Section 5(4)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross unearned income`                         IS A NUMBER
    `child support deducted under Section 5(3)(c) or (d)` IS A NUMBER
    `excluded income under Section 5(2)`            IS A NUMBER

-- Section 4(1): "The total gross non-KTAP income shall not exceed the gross income limitation standard", with the
-- Section 5 exclusions applied.
GIVEN i IS A `Monthly income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`gross non-KTAP income` i MEANS
    max 0 ((i's `gross earned income` PLUS i's `gross unearned income`) MINUS i's `excluded income under Section 5(2)`)

GIVEN i IS A `Monthly income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countable earned income` i MEANS
    IF i's `earnings deductions lost under Section 5(4)`
    THEN max 0 (i's `gross earned income`)
    ELSE IF i's `in the six months of the fifty percent disregard`
         THEN afterExpenses TIMES 0.5
         ELSE afterExpenses
    WHERE
        afterExpenses MEANS max 0 (i's `gross earned income` MINUS (175 TIMES i's `employed members of the benefit group`) MINUS i's `dependent care disregard`)

GIVEN i IS A `Monthly income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`countable income` i MEANS
    max 0 (`countable earned income` i
               PLUS (max 0 (i's `gross unearned income` MINUS i's `excluded income under Section 5(2)`))
               MINUS i's `child support deducted under Section 5(3)(c) or (d)`)

§§ `KRS 205.200(2); 921 KAR 2:016 Section 9(3) to (5) -- the payment`

-- 205.200(2): the secretary shall "allow for between a forty percent (40%) and a forty-five percent (45%) ratable
-- reduction ... In no instance shall grants to families with no income be less than the appropriate grant maximum".
-- Section 9(3): "a forty-five (45) percent ratable reduction shall be applied to the deficit between the family's
-- countable income and the standard of need". (4)(a): "The assistance payment shall be the lesser amount of either: 1.
-- Fifty-five (55) percent of the deficit ...; or 2. The payment maximum"; (b): for a family with no income it "shall be
-- calculated pursuant to KRS 205.200(2)" -- the payment maximum. (5): "If a benefit group's assistance payment equals zero
-- (0), the benefit group shall be ineligible". Section 4(2)(b): ineligible if countable income "exceeds the standard of
-- need".
DECLARE `KTAP result` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly KTAP payment of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `ineligible: resources over $10,000 (921 KAR 2:016 Section 3(2))`
    `ineligible: gross income over the gross income limit (Section 4(1)(c))`
    `ineligible: countable income over the standard of need (Section 4(2)(b))`
    `ineligible: the payment would be zero (Section 9(5))`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      `adjustment factor` IS A NUMBER
      i IS A `Monthly income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assistance payment` MEANS
    IF `gross non-KTAP income` i EQUALS 0
    THEN `payment maximum` n `adjustment factor`
    ELSE min (`payment maximum` n `adjustment factor`) (max 0 (0.55 TIMES (`standard of need` n `adjustment factor` MINUS `countable income` i)))

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      `adjustment factor` IS A NUMBER
      `countable liquid assets` IS A NUMBER
      i IS A `Monthly income`
GIVETH A `KTAP result`
`the KTAP determination` MEANS
    IF NOT (`is within the resource limitation` `countable liquid assets`)
    THEN `ineligible: resources over $10,000 (921 KAR 2:016 Section 3(2))`
    ELSE IF `gross non-KTAP income` i GREATER THAN `gross income limit` n `adjustment factor`
         THEN `ineligible: gross income over the gross income limit (Section 4(1)(c))`
         ELSE IF `countable income` i GREATER THAN `standard of need` n `adjustment factor`
              THEN `ineligible: countable income over the standard of need (Section 4(2)(b))`
              ELSE IF `the assistance payment` n `adjustment factor` i AT MOST 0
                   THEN `ineligible: the payment would be zero (Section 9(5))`
                   ELSE `a monthly KTAP payment of` (`the assistance payment` n `adjustment factor` i)

§§ `KRS 205.200(7) -- refusing work`

-- "No person shall be eligible for public assistance payments if, after having been determined to be potentially
-- responsible, and afforded notice and opportunity for hearing, he or she refuses without good cause: (a) To register for
-- employment with the state employment service, (b) To accept suitable training, or (c) To accept suitable employment."
GIVEN `determined potentially responsible and given notice and a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `refused to register for employment, accept suitable training, or accept suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred by 205.200(7)` IF
        `determined potentially responsible and given notice and a hearing`
    AND `refused to register for employment, accept suitable training, or accept suitable employment`
    AND (NOT `good cause`)

§§ `Duties`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the cabinet`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `report the increase in earnings`
    `use cash withdrawn with the EBT card other than for goods and services necessary for the welfare of the family`

-- 921 KAR 2:016 Section 5(4)(b): the earnings deductions are lost for a month in which the individual "Fails to report an
-- increase in earnings, that impacts eligibility, within ten (10) days of the change, unless good cause exists". Counted
-- in days from the change.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
DECIDE `the Section 5(4)(b) report of an increase in earnings` IS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `report the increase in earnings`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "the increase in earnings was not reported within ten days of the change: the work expense, dependent care and fifty percent deductions do not apply for that month, unless good cause exists (921 KAR 2:016 Section 5(4)(b))"

-- KRS 205.193(2): cash withdrawn with the EBT card "may only be used for goods and services necessary for the welfare of
-- the family, including but not limited to food, clothing, housing, utilities, child care, transportation, medicine, and
-- medical supplies". (3): recoupment, and the cabinet "may" fine up to $500 and disqualify for up to 1 month, 3 months,
-- 1 year.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
DECIDE `the 205.193(2) restriction on cash withdrawn` IS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    SHANT  `use cash withdrawn with the EBT card other than for goods and services necessary for the welfare of the family`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "cash withdrawn with the EBT card was used other than for goods and services necessary for the welfare of the family (KRS 205.193(2)); the cabinet seeks recoupment and may fine up to $500 and disqualify (205.193(3))"

-- 205.193(3)(b): the most the cabinet may disqualify for, by violation: 1 month, 3 months, 1 year (12 months).
GIVEN `which violation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most months of disqualification under 205.193(3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `which violation` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        IF `which violation` EQUALS 1 THEN 1
        IF `which violation` EQUALS 2 THEN 3
        OTHERWISE 12
